    "turn_idx": 77,
    "turn_text": "Well, I'm not sure you're right that one party's liberal and one party's conservative. I would argue that both of our political parties haven't been paying enough attention to the anger in the country about globalization and people dislocated by trade. I'm for trade, but I think each party has a more liberal and a more conservative wing or a more moderate and a more extreme wing, depending on how you want to call it, and that there has been a consensus in the country more or less in the middle for a long time. about how things should work, but now both edges are not happy with that. And I think Trump is reflecting the anger in parts of the Republican Party and Sanders reflected the anger in parts of the Democratic Party. And what worries me is that if we withdraw from the world and we say all trade is bad, I don't know that we'll get that. get to that point. What are we going to do? Flip burgers for each other? Who's going to",
